<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7901" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chrȳsa</span></b> , ae, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chrȳsē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χρύση</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town on the coast of Troas sacred to Apollo</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 30, 32, § 122</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1,
			18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13, 174</span></i> (cf. Hom. Il. 1, 390; 1,
			452).— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">An island near Crete</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				20, § 61</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An island of India</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 7,
			7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
